  <tr> 
    <td class="igtext" colspan="2"><a name="sysksu"></a><span class="igheader">Measuring 
      system </span><span class="igsmall">(KSU, 1989-1992)</span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr> 
    <td class="igtext" colspan="2"> 
      <p><span class="igsmall"><img src="electronics/sysksu4s.jpg" width="269" height="153" align="left"></span><span class="igsmall">Old 
        stuff but designed in a right way. I guess the similar system is still 
        in operation in KSU at X-band, and most probably I will be able to run 
        my one (Q-band, KSU) even now.The electrical/logical and mechanical specifications 
        of the system were introduced by B. Kazakov and I.Motygullin (MRS, KSU). 
        16-bit bi-directional data bus, (4+8) bits address space, 4 bits for slot 
        address. 20 slots in crate, 16 out of them are programmable. Priority 
        interrupt controller, crate controller, address decoder and link to ISA. 
        Fully featured/very powerful system and what is even more important- it's 
        simple enough to be build by non-engineer.</span></p>
      <p><a href="#tech">back</a></p>
      <p class="igsmall">&nbsp;</p>
